hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15836","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi informed him that Isa ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydillah informed him that Umayr ibn Salamah al-Damri informed him, from a man of Bahz, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heading for Makkah, until when they were in part of Wadi al-Rawha the people found a wild donkey hamstrung, and they mentioned it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Leave it until its owner comes. So the Bahzi came, and he was its owner, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, dispose of this donkey as you wish. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Abu Bakr, and he divided it among the companies while they were in ihram. He said: Then we passed on until when we were at al-Uthayah, there was a gazelle crouching in a shade with an arrow in it, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded a man to stand by it until the people passed beyond it."
